          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "user-f123ca2978@example.invalid",
          "hideComponent": "false",
          "jcr:created": "Thu Sep 10 2020 13:09:36 GMT+0000",
          "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
          "text": "<h1><span style=\"color: #1c5687;\"><span style=\"color: #4c7d7a;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"color: #ffb500;\"><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-5em\">Strategies for Reducing Falls in the ED</span></span></span></span></span></span></h1>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">As more and more patients enter the hospital through the ED, emergency nurses are not only tasked with saving lives in emergencies – but they’re also responsible for keeping patients safe from adverse outcomes such as falls. In this educational webinar we will share eye-opening statistics, discuss human and financial costs of falls, identify risk factors and interventions, and focus on evidence-based practices in the utilization of technology for prevention of patient falls.<br>\n</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\"><b>Course Objectives:</b></span></p>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Distinguish between the different types of falls</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Discuss human and financial costs of a fall</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Identify ED-specific risk factors for falls</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Discuss evidence-based fall prevention practices in the emergency department</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Discuss integration of technology into fall and injury prevention practices</span></li>\n</ul>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Wed Sep 03 2025 13:30:50 GMT+0000",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "rightPadding": "2",
          "backgroundColor": "rgba(255,255,255,0)",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      }
    },
